<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#transhumance">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transhumance</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Transhumance is the seasonal movement of livestock and herders between different pastures, typically between lowland winter grazing and highland summer grazing. It was common in mountainous regions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">ancient Near East</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> practised transhumance <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pastoralism">pastoralism</a> alongside sedentary farming, creating a diversified economy resilient to climatic variability.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transhumance.jpg" alt="Transhumance" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CamDib · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Transumanza_nel_Parc_National_des_Ecrins.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
